 "verdict_reason": "Technical split-half passes (0.86/0.85), but scoring one batch's WT arm against another's (no query at all) reproduces 83% of the z<=-3 and 51% of the z<=-4 hit rate of the real query screens, the same library genes (PRDX1, DDX19A, PPP2R3C, C17orf70, BRIP1) come up for 5-6 unrelated queries across batches, known controls are absent (ARID1A-ARID1B z=+1.5), the hit rate at a null-calibrated cut-off is implausibly low (0.08%, 187 pos), and different-line overlap with desjardins2026 on STK11/ARID1A is at chance (0.51/0.46). Measurements (z) are kept; labels should not be used."
